1
00:00:00,550 --> 00:00:06,702
This tutorial shows how to read the check-in kiosk logs in the What-If Tool: where drivers spend

2
00:00:06,702 --> 00:00:09,650
their time, and how the AI assistant can help.

3
00:00:10,950 --> 00:00:16,530
Before entering the yard, every driver checks in at a self-service kiosk,

4
00:00:16,530 --> 00:00:20,352
which logs each screen as a German status message.

5
00:00:20,352 --> 00:00:27,843
The tool groups 5,764 of those messages into 34 driver visits, translates every step into English,

6
00:00:27,843 --> 00:00:30,900
and measures how long each screen takes.

7
00:00:32,200 --> 00:00:35,362
Start with the plain-English summary at the top.

8
00:00:35,362 --> 00:00:39,182
It is written straight from the data, with no AI involved.

9
00:00:39,182 --> 00:00:45,900
A typical visit takes two minutes 25 seconds, and 8 of the 34 visits never reached the closing screen.

10
00:00:47,200 --> 00:00:52,949
Below it, five key numbers give the scale: 34 visits, 5,764 events,

11
00:00:52,949 --> 00:01:00,500
the typical visit length with its slow tail, events per visit, and 21 different screens.

12
00:01:01,800 --> 00:01:05,142
The time per step chart ranks the slowest screens.

13
00:01:05,142 --> 00:01:09,821
The solid bar is the typical time, and the faded bar is the slow tail.

14
00:01:09,821 --> 00:01:16,706
Choosing a language normally takes 41 seconds, but the slowest visits stay on it for almost 40 minutes.

15
00:01:16,706 --> 00:01:20,850
Hover over a bar to see the German screen name and both times.

16
00:01:22,150 --> 00:01:25,566
Click a visit in the sessions table to open it.

17
00:01:25,566 --> 00:01:27,528
Visit 1420 took 41 minutes.

18
00:01:27,528 --> 00:01:33,415
The bar at the top, Where did the time go, shows that 97 percent went into setup,

19
00:01:33,415 --> 00:01:36,322
almost all of it on the language screen.

20
00:01:36,322 --> 00:01:40,900
Names and signatures stay masked unless you click Reveal P I I.

21
00:01:42,200 --> 00:01:47,515
Every step is listed with its English name and the German kiosk name underneath.

22
00:01:47,515 --> 00:01:49,243
Click a step to expand it.

23
00:01:49,243 --> 00:01:55,156
You see its phase, whether it is a screen the driver uses, the exact start and end times,

24
00:01:55,156 --> 00:01:56,950
and the raw kiosk messages.

25
00:01:58,250 --> 00:02:04,988
The round button in the bottom-right corner opens the AI assistant, which runs locally on your machine.

26
00:02:04,988 --> 00:02:07,801
We asked which screen has the longest tail.

27
00:02:07,801 --> 00:02:12,773
It named the language screen, quoted the real figures, and suggested causes,

28
00:02:12,773 --> 00:02:16,175
such as drivers being unsure which language to pick.

29
00:02:17,475 --> 00:02:20,144
It also reads the visit you have open.

30
00:02:20,144 --> 00:02:26,818
For visit 1420, it confirmed the driver finished, and pointed to the 39 minutes spent in setup.

31
00:02:26,818 --> 00:02:31,525
Treat its reasons as ideas, and check its numbers against the page.

32
00:02:32,825 --> 00:02:33,421
To recap.

33
00:02:33,421 --> 00:02:35,869
Start with the plain-English summary.

34
00:02:35,869 --> 00:02:39,310
Look for long faded bars in the time per step chart.

35
00:02:39,310 --> 00:02:42,288
Keep personal data masked unless you need it.

36
00:02:42,288 --> 00:02:45,200
And check what the AI says against the page.

37
00:02:46,500 --> 00:02:50,671
For every step in more detail, see the check-in logs user guide.

38
00:02:50,671 --> 00:02:51,975
Thanks for watching.
